# Initialize Transaction

Use this endpoint to start a new payment transaction. Calling this endpoint returns an `authorization_url` where you redirect the customer to complete their payment on Paystack's secure checkout page.

{% endpoint method="POST" path="/transaction/initialize" /%}

{% callout type="info" title="Authentication Required" %}
All requests to the Paystack API require authorization via your secret key. Include your key in the HTTP Header as `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_SECRET_KEY`.
{% /callout %}

{% callout type="tip" title="Interactive API Console" %}
Use the sticky API Explorer console on the right panel to test live requests with custom payloads and your secret key (`sk_test_...`).
{% /callout %}

---

## Request Body Parameters

Use these parameters in your JSON payload when invoking the endpoint:

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `email` | `string` | **Required** | Customer's email address. Used for payment notifications and receipts. |
| `amount` | `integer` | **Required** | Amount in subunit of currency (e.g., kobo for NGN). `20000` = ₦200.00. |
| `currency` | `string` | Optional | Currency code (`NGN`, `GHS`, `ZAR`, `USD`). Default: `NGN`. |
| `reference` | `string` | Optional | Unique transaction reference. Auto-generated if omitted. |
| `callback_url` | `string` | Optional | Fully qualified URL where customer is redirected after payment. |
| `plan` | `string` | Optional | Subscription plan code if initializing a recurring payment. |

---

## Integration Code Example

Here is how you initialize a transaction using Node.js:

```javascript
const paystack = require('paystack')('sk_test_YOUR_SECRET_KEY');

paystack.transaction.initialize({
  email: 'customer@example.com',
  amount: 20000, // ₦200.00
  currency: 'NGN'
})
.then((response) => {
  console.log('Authorization URL:', response.data.authorization_url);
})
.catch((error) => {
  console.error(error);
});
```

---

## Response Reference

### `200 OK` (Success)

When a transaction is successfully initialized, Paystack returns a `200 OK` status with the customer checkout URL:

```json
{
  "status": true,
  "message": "Authorization URL created",
  "data": {
    "authorization_url": "https://checkout.paystack.com/08611130388d55c",
    "access_code": "08611130388d55c",
    "reference": "7PV9766bsq"
  }
}
```

{% callout type="tip" title="Webhooks & Verification" %}
Always listen to the `charge.success` webhook event or verify the transaction using `GET /transaction/verify/:reference` before delivering value to your customer.
{% /callout %}
